## Approach

- Initialize `left` and `right` pointers.
- Calculate the middle element of the current range.
- If `nums[mid]` is equal to the target, return `mid`.
- Check which half of the array is sorted.
- If the left half is sorted, check if the target lies in that range.
- Otherwise, search in the right half.
- If the right half is sorted, check if the target lies in that range.
- Keep moving `left` or `right` until the target is found.
- Return `-1` if the target is not present.
